IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g5-interpretation.l4: the fork points of group G5 (Articles 13 and 14 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) in the R4 shape.
-- One fork point is one enumeration with one constructor per reading; every fork point is a field of the ONE record
-- `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`, `TYPICALLY` the reading taken.  Every public decision of g5-art13-effects and
-- g5-art14-court-powers that depends on a fork takes that record as an ordinary GIVEN and delegates by CONSIDER to one private
-- implementation per reading, so each reading is a callable function with its own test.
-- The register of the forks (id, provision, the text that licenses each reading, the reading taken and why, the discriminating case)
-- is in FRAGMENT-G5.md; the ids F5.1 to F5.14 below map 1:1 to the fields of the record.
-- Nothing here is a rule: the module holds only the readings.  It imports domain only for the enumeration
-- `Meaning of the year of an annual return` (fork F5.2), which G3 types its own field with too (integration point IP33).

§ `Fork points of Articles 13 and 14`

-- F5.1  Article 13(6): "must promptly report".  "Promptly" is a standard of promptness and states no number (period P8).
DECLARE `Measure of promptness under Article 13(6)` IS ONE OF
    `an input judgement that the report was made promptly`
    `a number of days from the event or proposal` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc Days allowed to report, counted from the event or proposal; the Law states no number, so the caller supplies it
    `a number of days from the charity becoming aware of the matter` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc Days allowed to report, counted from the day the charity became aware of the matter; the Law states no number, so the caller supplies it

-- F5.3  Article 13(10): "any Order under paragraph (7), (8) or (9)".  Paragraph (8) confers no Order of its own (trap T18).
DECLARE `Meaning of an Order under paragraph (8) in Article 13(10)` IS ONE OF
    `the Order under paragraph (7) as extended by paragraph (8)`
    `no Order exists under paragraph (8)`

-- F5.4  Article 14(1)(a): "misconduct in the administration of the charity".
DECLARE `Meaning of misconduct in the administration of the charity` IS ONE OF
    `misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity`
    `any misconduct within Article 2(10)`
    `misconduct in the ordinary sense, not the defined term`

-- F5.5  Article 13(8): is an annual return sent on the due date set by an Order timely (period P10)?
DECLARE `Whether a return sent on the due date is timely` IS ONE OF
    `timely if sent on or before the due date`
    `late unless sent before the due date`

-- F5.6  Article 13(1): the day on which deregistration takes effect, as an edge of the period during which paragraphs (2) to (4) apply.
DECLARE `Whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the period of registration` IS ONE OF
    `outside: registered up to the day before deregistration takes effect`
    `inside: registered up to and including the day deregistration takes effect`

-- F5.7  Article 13(2): "a purpose that is not charitable", read with Article 5(1)(a)(ii) (purposes purely ancillary or incidental).
DECLARE `Meaning of a purpose that is not charitable in Article 13(2)` IS ONE OF
    `any purpose that is not a charitable purpose under Article 6, a purely ancillary purpose included`
    `a purpose that is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one`

-- F5.8  Article 13(5): how paragraphs (a) and (b), joined by "or", combine.
DECLARE `How paragraphs (a) and (b) of Article 13(5) combine` IS ONE OF
    `either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition`
    `once permission is given the different condition replaces the original condition`

-- F5.9  Article 14(3)(a), (b) and (g): "a specified period" fixed by the court (the order names a first day and a length).
DECLARE `Whether the first day named counts in a period fixed by the court` IS ONE OF
    `the first day named is the first day of the period`
    `the period starts on the day after the first day named`

-- F5.10  Article 13(6): when "promptly" is read as a number of days (readings 2 and 3 of F5.1), is the day of the event counted?
DECLARE `Whether the day of the event counts in the number of days for a report` IS ONE OF
    `the day of the event is not counted: the last prompt day is the event day plus the number of days`
    `the day of the event is the first day: the last prompt day is one day earlier`

-- F5.11  Article 13(7): when the year of a return is the twelve months from each anniversary of registration (reading 3 of F5.2),
-- what is the anniversary of a registration made on 29 February?
DECLARE `Anniversary of a registration made on 29 February` IS ONE OF
    `the last day of February (the day is clamped, as daydate add years does)`
    `the first day of March (the day rolls forward)`

-- F5.12  Article 14(2): "to remedy the misconduct, protect the property and secure its proper application".
DECLARE `Purposes an order under Article 14(2) must serve` IS ONE OF
    `at least one of the three purposes`
    `all three purposes`

-- F5.13  Article 13(7): "any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year": which date is the date the matter arises?
DECLARE `Date on which a matter arises for the annual return` IS ONE OF
    `the date of the event or proposal`
    `the date the charity became aware of the matter`

-- F5.14  Article 13(11)(a): "a statement provided under paragraph (9)(b)".  Paragraph (11)(b) speaks of permission to amend "that statement", and
-- paragraph (9)(b) of a statement of "current intentions"; the Law does not say which of several statements, provided over time, a payment is judged by.
DECLARE `Statement that a payment must be consistent with` IS ONE OF
    `the statement in force on the day of the payment`
    `any statement provided on or before the day of the payment`

§ `The record that carries them`

DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
    HAS `how promptness is measured` IS A `Measure of promptness under Article 13(6)`
            TYPICALLY `an input judgement that the report was made promptly`
        `the meaning of the year of an annual return` IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return`
            TYPICALLY `the calendar year`
        `the meaning of an Order under paragraph (8)` IS A `Meaning of an Order under paragraph (8) in Article 13(10)`
            TYPICALLY `the Order under paragraph (7) as extended by paragraph (8)`
        `the meaning of misconduct in the administration` IS A `Meaning of misconduct in the administration of the charity`
            TYPICALLY `misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity`
        `whether a return sent on the due date is timely` IS A `Whether a return sent on the due date is timely`
            TYPICALLY `timely if sent on or before the due date`
        `whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the registration` IS A `Whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the period of registration`
            TYPICALLY `outside: registered up to the day before deregistration takes effect`
        `the meaning of a purpose that is not charitable` IS A `Meaning of a purpose that is not charitable in Article 13(2)`
            TYPICALLY `any purpose that is not a charitable purpose under Article 6, a purely ancillary purpose included`
        `how the two paragraphs of Article 13(5) combine` IS A `How paragraphs (a) and (b) of Article 13(5) combine`
            TYPICALLY `either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition`
        `whether the first day counts in a period fixed by the court` IS A `Whether the first day named counts in a period fixed by the court`
            TYPICALLY `the first day named is the first day of the period`
        `whether the day of the event counts in a number of days` IS A `Whether the day of the event counts in the number of days for a report`
            TYPICALLY `the day of the event is not counted: the last prompt day is the event day plus the number of days`
        `the anniversary of a registration made on 29 February` IS AN `Anniversary of a registration made on 29 February`
            TYPICALLY `the last day of February (the day is clamped, as daydate add years does)`
        `the purposes an order under Article 14(2) must serve` IS A `Purposes an order under Article 14(2) must serve`
            TYPICALLY `at least one of the three purposes`
        `the date on which a matter arises` IS A `Date on which a matter arises for the annual return`
            TYPICALLY `the date of the event or proposal`
        `the statement a payment must be consistent with` IS A `Statement that a payment must be consistent with`
            TYPICALLY `the statement in force on the day of the payment`

-- The readings taken, as a value to hand to a public decision.  Each of the other readings of a fork point is a named variant below,
-- so a test can call the alternative without writing the whole record.
`the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` WITH
        `how promptness is measured` IS `an input judgement that the report was made promptly`
        `the meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
        `the meaning of an Order under paragraph (8)` IS `the Order under paragraph (7) as extended by paragraph (8)`
        `the meaning of misconduct in the administration` IS `misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity`
        `whether a return sent on the due date is timely` IS `timely if sent on or before the due date`
        `whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the registration` IS `outside: registered up to the day before deregistration takes effect`
        `the meaning of a purpose that is not charitable` IS `any purpose that is not a charitable purpose under Article 6, a purely ancillary purpose included`
        `how the two paragraphs of Article 13(5) combine` IS `either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition`
        `whether the first day counts in a period fixed by the court` IS `the first day named is the first day of the period`
        `whether the day of the event counts in a number of days` IS `the day of the event is not counted: the last prompt day is the event day plus the number of days`
        `the anniversary of a registration made on 29 February` IS `the last day of February (the day is clamped, as daydate add years does)`
        `the purposes an order under Article 14(2) must serve` IS `at least one of the three purposes`
        `the date on which a matter arises` IS `the date of the event or proposal`
        `the statement a payment must be consistent with` IS `the statement in force on the day of the payment`

